    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build is clean. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>` \u2014 REGION derived from the postcode, HASH8 the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`, with sequence numbers gone. Everything downstream of the customer code moved onto that new identity.\n\n**New, single-responsibility units in `model/`** (alongside the existing `CheckDigit`, `Locality`, `OwnerIdentity`):\n- `Sha256.upperHex(value, length)` \u2014 the one definition of a truncated upper-case-hex SHA-256 fingerprint. `OwnerHouseholds.householdId` now reuses it, so its hand-rolled digest loop is gone (behaviour preserved exactly \u2014 including its pre-existing NUL-byte key separator).\n- `CustomerCode` \u2014 owns the `<REGION>-<HASH8>` format in one place: `forOwner(owner)` builds it, `region(code)` reads the region back out. Building and parsing living together means the format can't drift.\n\n**Wiring the new identity through:**\n- `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` now just calls `CustomerCode.forOwner(owner)` \u2014 no more repository, no per-city sequence.\n- `OwnerMapper.locality` now returns `CustomerCode.region(owner.getCustomerCode())` instead of independently recomputing from city/postcode, so locality *is* the identity's region (single source of truth).\n- `membershipNumber`, `checkDigit`, and the create audit record already read `customerCode`, so they automatically carry the new identity \u2014 no logic duplicated.\n- `Locality` gained a clean postcode-only `regionForPostcode(...)` and shed the now-obsolete postcode-then-city `regionFor(city, postcode)`.\n\n**Docs:** updated the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality` descriptions/examples in `openapi.yml`, plus stale javadocs in `OwnerCities`/`RejectFullOwnerCity`.\n\n## Verification\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` passes (audit log confirms e.g. `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`).\n- Full `./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, all tests green.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: REGION is derived strictly from the postcode per the spec's wording (\"derived from the postcode\"), so an owner with no/unknown postcode now gets region `UNKNOWN` in both the customer code and locality \u2014 previously locality fell back to the city table. No existing test relied on that fallback.",
